From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: apply Sheng WCN7850 firmware workarounds

Porting notes: Scope the fork rfkill-pin bypass and single-chip MLO workaround to the Sheng WCN7850. The packaged amss.bin identifies itself as WLAN.HMT.1.1.c2-00259, the firmware version named by the MLO source commit. Other machines retain 7.3 behavior.

Original author dates, messages, and trailers: patches/ORIGINS.md.
Source-Commit: https://github.com/ianchb/sm8550-mainline/commit/980c62590f0f883647fa13a80d0be27e61c654e5
Source-Commit: https://github.com/ianchb/sm8550-mainline/commit/65ff5f4fe0963dcf91e6e94c6d0d6d38432dfb50
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index 262a204..8a52422 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -82,6 +82,10 @@ static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;
+	/* Sheng's WCN7850 has no working rfkill GPIO; preserve other boards. */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20 &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,sheng"))
+		return 0;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
 		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 280e50a..46ff515 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2357,7 +2357,9 @@ static void ath12k_qmi_phy_cap_send(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	if (resp.single_chip_mlo_support_valid && resp.single_chip_mlo_support)
+	if ((resp.single_chip_mlo_support_valid && resp.single_chip_mlo_support) ||
+	    (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20 &&
+	     of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,sheng")))
 		ab->single_chip_mlo_support = true;
 
 	if (!resp.num_phy_valid) {
